                <pb facs="0806" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 195.2/258</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-11T10:00:00+02:30">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 11, 1914, 10 a.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>12. Reported plan of allowing Americans to purchase German vessels causing most
                    unfavorable comment here, official and in the press. Public opinion already
                    believes that American Government has pro-German sympathies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
